{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775377342-4MteG4ctYSgDPusfGckV","role":"assistant","created":1775377349,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the task:\n\n1. I need to find the nominal average bank discount rates from the U.S. Treasury's Financing Operations reported in the June 1980 bulletin\n2. For two Cash Management Treasury bills:\n   - 19-day bills with tenders opened on May 27, 1980\n   - 2-day bills with tenders opened on June 2, 1980\n3. Then compute the one step realized variance of the log average bank discount rate\n4. Output the value rounded to the nearest hundredths place as a decimal value\n\nLet me first look at the available resources to find this data.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_e32f7f76004dd04d","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [ ] Find 19-day bills with tenders opened on May 27, 1980 in the Treasury bulletin\n- [ ] Find 2-day bills with tenders opened on June 2, 1980 in the Treasury bulletin\n- [ ] Extract the nominal average bank discount rates for both\n- [ ] Compute the one step realized variance of the log average bank discount rate\n- [ ] Output the result to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
